From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DarekM <149845949+aninmucek@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:08:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: Add Pixel 8a (akita) first-light
 board

Add a first-light board file for the Pixel 8a: husky's first-light file
with akita's model, compatible and /soc_compatible children, and USB.
zuma.dtsi already describes the first DRAM bank (ABL adds the others),
the fixed reservations, the watchdogs, and the PMU with its reboot
mode; this file switches on the DWC3 and its two PHYs and carries
husky's bootargs.

akita's ABL picks the base DTB by /soc_compatible, as husky's does, but
a retail 8a has the IPOP package: its live tree's children are B0_IPOP
and B1_IPOP (product id 0x9865, pkg_mode 1), the two that Google's
zuma-b0-ipop.dts carries, where husky's are FOPLP.

Every fixed DRAM reservation in the 8a's live tree lies inside one of
zuma.dtsi's, at husky's addresses, except the four that ABL inserts
itself (pkvm_guest_firmware, sec_dram, sec_pt and
debug_kinfo_reserved). The DWC3, the USB DRD PHY, the UART, the PMU and
the watchdogs are at zuma.dtsi's addresses.

There is no framebuffer yet: the splash address is read from DPP0 on a
running 8a before a carve-out goes in, as on husky. UFS, the buttons,
the PMICs, touch and the MAX77759 follow, each once it has run on the
phone.

Tested on a Pixel 8a (bootloader akita-17.0-15681527): the bootloader
boots this tree from slot B, all nine CPUs come up, the watchdog
driver stops both cluster watchdogs, and the initramfs brings up the
USB gadget and SSH 0.4 s into boot. The booted tree has the
bootloader's DRAM banks and its four reservations added, and the
kernel reports no reserved-memory overlap.

Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/devices/google/akita/+/refs/tags/android-16.0.0_r0.10/dts/zuma-akita-mp.dts
Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/devices/google/zuma/+/refs/tags/android-16.0.0_r0.10/dts/zuma-b0-ipop.dts
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: DarekM <149845949+aninmucek@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/Makefile    |  2 +
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts     | 61 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 63 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/Makefile
index 8e651de7d..3f8e377c7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/Makefile
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@ dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_EXYNOS) += \
 	gs201-felix.dtb \
 	gs201-lynx.dtb \
 	gs201-panther.dtb \
+	zuma-akita.dtb \
 	zuma-husky.dtb \
 	zumapro-tegu.dtb
 
@@ -19,5 +20,6 @@ DTC_FLAGS_gs201-cheetah += -@
 DTC_FLAGS_gs201-felix += -@
 DTC_FLAGS_gs201-lynx += -@
 DTC_FLAGS_gs201-panther += -@
+DTC_FLAGS_zuma-akita += -@
 DTC_FLAGS_zuma-husky += -@
 DTC_FLAGS_zumapro-tegu += -@
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..8aadf4edc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+/*
+ * Google Pixel 8a (akita) - first-light board file.
+ */
+
+/dts-v1/;
+
+#include "zuma.dtsi"
+
+/ {
+	model = "Google Pixel 8a";
+	compatible = "google,zuma-akita", "google,zuma";
+
+	/*
+	 * zuma's ABL picks the base DTB by matching these children against
+	 * the SoC's product id, revision and package; there is no /soc_id.
+	 * A retail akita has a B0/B1 IPOP part (stock base DTB 3, which
+	 * carries exactly these two), where husky's is FOPLP.
+	 */
+	soc_compatible {
+		B0_IPOP {
+			product_id = <0x9865>;
+			major = <1>;
+			minor = <0>;
+			pkg_mode = <1>;
+		};
+
+		B1_IPOP {
+			product_id = <0x9865>;
+			major = <1>;
+			minor = <1>;
+			pkg_mode = <1>;
+		};
+	};
+
+	chosen {
+		/*
+		 * ABL requires bootargs to exist; it appends its own after these.
+		 * reboot=warm: a cold PSCI reset clears the reboot reason in
+		 * SYSIP_DAT0 before ABL reads it, so "reboot bootloader" would
+		 * only boot the slot again.
+		 * The watchdog driver stops the bootloader's watchdogs, so a
+		 * hang that never panics lasts until someone resets the phone
+		 * with its buttons: panic on soft and hard lockups and on RCU
+		 * stalls, so that panic=10 resets the phone by itself.
+		 */
+		bootargs = "console=tty0 fbcon=font:TER16x32 reboot=warm panic=10 softlockup_panic=1 nmi_watchdog=panic sysctl.kernel.panic_on_rcu_stall=1 clk_ignore_unused pd_ignore_unused rdinit=/init";
+	};
+};
+
+&usb_dwc3 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&usb_hsphy {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&usbdrd_phy {
+	status = "okay";
+};
